--- field object.network.id
type: str
asserted: true

The Registry network record identifier whose Connect descriptor radiusd checked.

Copied from radiusd's audit context by the kernel. The object kind is `network`;
its access mask defines Connect as bit 0 (0x1). This is a configuration identity,
not a kernel-observed network or proof that the supplied descriptor belongs to it.

--- field object.network.ssid
type: str
asserted: true

The network's SSID as a display label, copied from radiusd's audit context.

Invalid UTF-8 bytes are replaced with U+FFFD for display. This label never
selects policy; radiusd binds the exchange using the original SSID bytes and
identifies the configuration with `object.network.id`.

--- field source.radiusd.username
type: str

The inner PAP or MSCHAPv2 username supplied before identity verification.

This is unverified input, including on success. It is not a SID or proof of
identity. It can contain a typing mistake or arbitrary peer-controlled text.

--- field object.radiusd.canonical-name
type: str

The canonical account name returned after authd verified the requested credential.

--- field object.radiusd.attempt.guid
type: bin.guid

The random identifier of the short-lived authentication conversation.

--- field object.radiusd.client.id
type: uint

The first eight bytes of SHA-256 of the client record name, as a big-endian integer.

This identifies configuration, not an AP's asserted NAS identity.

--- field object.radiusd.network.id
type: uint

The first eight bytes of SHA-256 of the network record name, as a big-endian integer.

--- field object.radiusd.progress.sequence
type: uint

The one-based milestone sequence within an attempt.

Missing numbers indicate incomplete evidence. The final summary has the next sequence number, including milestones omitted by the stage bound.

--- field object.radiusd.progress.result
type: str.enum
values: observed | offered | selected | pending | established | verified | failed | granted | refused | authentication-failed | permission-denied | missing-context | authority-unavailable | kernel-api-unavailable | access-check-error | conversation-limit | timed-out | binding-changed | protocol-error | undelivered | allowance-exhausted | accounting-unavailable | tls-failed | protocol-failed
closed: false

The stage result or final conversation outcome.

A successful request or method offer does not mean admission was granted.

--- field object.radiusd.progress.stage
type: str

The observed stage of the authentication conversation.

Values include started, method, tls, credentials, permissions, assignment, accounting and completed.

--- field object.radiusd.last-stage
type: str

The last observed stage before the conversation ended.

This describes progress, not an inferred cause of missing client activity.

--- field object.radiusd.method
type: str

The offered or selected EAP method.

The stage distinguishes an offer from an observed client selection.

--- field object.radiusd.elapsed-ms
type: uint

The elapsed monotonic time since conversation allocation, in milliseconds.

--- field object.radiusd.retransmissions
type: uint

The number of exact cached-request retransmissions observed during the attempt.

Terminal retransmissions after the attempt ended do not update its completed summary.

--- field object.radiusd.listener
type: str

The local configured UDP socket address for the conversation.

--- field object.radiusd.listener-index
type: uint

The zero-based listener index in the active configuration.

This index is meaningful within that configuration, not a persistent listener identity.

--- field source.radiusd.station
type: str

The normalized station MAC address asserted by the trusted client.

An AP assertion is not independent proof of a device's identity.

--- field object.radiusd.client.configuration-id
type: str

The client configuration record identifier selected by radiusd.

Matching an address to configuration does not establish packet integrity.

--- field object.radiusd.network.configuration-id
type: str

The access-policy configuration record identifier selected for the network.

This is the stable configuration GUID, separate from the legacy numeric network identifier.

--- field object.radiusd.authentication-profile.id
type: str

The authentication-profile configuration record identifier.

--- field object.radiusd.config.fingerprint
type: str

The effective authentication configuration fingerprint observed for the stage.

Display labels and diagnostic controls are excluded. Historical decisions are not recomputed using present configuration.

--- field object.radiusd.config.saved-fingerprint
type: str

The saved configuration fingerprint observed for the stage.

This differs from the effective authentication fingerprint and can change for display-only edits.

--- field object.radiusd.assignment.rule.id
type: str

The rule configuration identifier that selected the assignment.

--- field object.radiusd.assignment.profile.id
type: str

The access-profile configuration identifier selected by assignment.

--- field object.radiusd.assignment.vlan
type: uint

The VLAN selected by assignment, in the range 1–4094.

A later admission failure can prevent it from being sent. This does not prove an AP applied the VLAN or a device renewed its address.

--- field object.radiusd.assignment.fingerprint
type: str

SHA-256 of the selected VLAN and complete compiled authorization settings.
This identifies logical settings and equipment encodings without publishing
their values. A later admission failure can prevent delivery; it does not
establish that network equipment enforced the settings.

--- field object.radiusd.reply
type: str

The final local reply submission result.

Values are accept-submitted, reject-submitted, send-failed and none. Submission does not prove delivery or connectivity.

--- field object.radiusd.diagnostics.truncated
type: bool

Whether the producer omitted diagnostic stages or summary fields to satisfy its bounds.

Absence does not prove complete collection.

--- field object.radiusd.drops.count
type: uint

The number of discarded requests in one listener-and-reason report interval.

Optional source and client fields describe one bounded sample, not every counted request.

--- field object.radiusd.diagnostics.emitted
type: uint

The cumulative number of diagnostic events accepted by local event submission.

This is not an acknowledgment of persistent storage or delivery to a reader.

--- field object.radiusd.diagnostics.failed
type: uint

The cumulative number of diagnostic events refused by schema, size or submission checks.

--- field object.radiusd.diagnostics.suppressed
type: uint

The cumulative number of diagnostic events omitted by the local emission budget.

--- field object.radiusd.diagnostics.disabled
type: uint

The cumulative number of admitted diagnostic emissions omitted by event policy.

Events suppressed by the budget are counted separately before event policy is checked.

--- field object.radiusd.diagnostics.report-seconds
type: uint

The configured interval between diagnostic collection reports, in seconds.

Counters are cumulative since daemon startup; drop counts cover the preceding report interval.

--- field object.radiusd.client.name
type: str

The client display label observed when the conversation was allocated.

This historical label does not select policy or establish identity.

--- field object.radiusd.network.name
type: str

The access-policy display label observed when the conversation was allocated.

This historical label does not select policy or establish identity.

--- field object.radiusd.authentication-profile.name
type: str

The authentication-profile display label observed when the conversation was allocated.

This historical label does not select policy or establish identity.

--- field object.radiusd.assignment.profile.name
type: str

The access-profile display label observed during assignment evaluation.

This historical label does not select policy or establish identity.

--- field object.radiusd.assignment.rule.name
type: str

The winning rule display label observed during assignment evaluation.

This historical label does not select policy or establish identity.

--- group object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

Observed authentication context, subject to diagnostic bounds and field access.

field: subject.token.sid required
field: object.radiusd.attempt.guid required
field: object.radiusd.progress.sequence required
field: object.radiusd.progress.stage required
field: outcome.success required
field: object.radiusd.progress.result required
field: object.radiusd.client.name optional
field: object.radiusd.network.name optional
field: object.radiusd.authentication-profile.name optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.profile.name optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.rule.name optional
field: outcome.reason optional
  values: authentication-failed | permission-denied | missing-context | authority-unavailable | kernel-api-unavailable | access-check-error | conversation-limit | timed-out | binding-changed | protocol-error | undelivered | allowance-exhausted | accounting-unavailable | tls-failed | protocol-failed
  closed: false
field: outcome.detail optional
field: source.address optional
field: source.radiusd.username optional
field: source.radiusd.station optional
field: object.radiusd.listener optional
field: object.radiusd.canonical-name optional
field: object.account.sid optional
field: object.authentication.operation.guid optional
field: object.radiusd.client.configuration-id optional
field: object.radiusd.network.configuration-id optional
field: object.radiusd.authentication-profile.id optional
field: object.radiusd.config.fingerprint optional
field: object.radiusd.config.saved-fingerprint optional
field: object.radiusd.method optional
field: object.radiusd.elapsed-ms optional
field: object.radiusd.retransmissions optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.rule.id optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.profile.id optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.fingerprint optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.vlan optional
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.truncated optional

--- event radiusd.exchange.started
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

A server authentication conversation was allocated.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.method.offered
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

An EAP method was offered to the client.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.method.selected
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

A client selected an offered EAP method.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.tls.negotiated
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

TLS tunnel negotiation completed or failed.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.credential.requested
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

Credential verification was requested.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.credential.verified
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

An authd credential verification completed.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.permission.checked
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

The network Connect permission was checked.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.assignment.evaluated
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

The assignment policy was evaluated.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.accounting.requested
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

Accounting admission was requested.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.accounting.checked
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

Accounting admission completed.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.exchange.protocol.checked
tier: standard
gating: allocated conversations and the configured diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per distinct stage result and effective authentication configuration

A protocol processing failure was observed.

This is one observed action, not the final conversation outcome. A successful
request or offer does not mean credentials were verified or access was granted.
Milestones are best effort; the final exchange summary can survive their loss.

include: object.radiusd.diagnostic-context

--- event radiusd.request.discarded
tier: standard
gating: discarded requests grouped by listener and reason at the report interval
cardinality: one bounded report per listener-and-reason bucket

Requests were discarded without completing a server authentication attempt.

Counts aggregate requests, not identities. Optional source and matched client
fields represent a bounded recent sample. Integrity failure does not establish
that a configured shared secret was wrong. These reports are not attempt rows.

field: subject.token.sid required
field: object.radiusd.listener-index required
field: object.radiusd.drops.count required
field: outcome.success required
  Always false.
field: outcome.reason required
  values: unknown-client | disabled-client | malformed-request | integrity-failed | unknown-state | stale-binding | client-mismatch | network-mismatch | configuration-unavailable | missing-network | network-not-permitted | disabled-network | tls-configuration | conversation-limit | binding-mismatch | protocol-rejected
  closed: false
field: source.address optional
field: object.radiusd.client.configuration-id optional

--- event radiusd.diagnostics.reported
tier: standard
gating: the configured report interval and diagnostic emission bounds
cardinality: once per report interval when emission is available

Diagnostic collection counters were sampled.

Counters accumulate since daemon startup. The sample precedes its own emission.
Successful local submission does not prove persistent eventd storage. Reporting
is itself best effort and does not alter authentication decisions.

field: subject.token.sid required
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.emitted required
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.failed required
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.suppressed required
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.disabled required
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.report-seconds required

--- event radiusd.exchange.attempted
tier: standard
gating: integrity-checked exchanges allocated a server conversation
cardinality: once when the logical conversation terminates; retransmissions write none

A RADIUS authentication conversation ended.

Success means that current network policy granted Connect and the UDP socket
accepted the Access-Accept for transmission. It does not prove that the AP
received it or admitted a device. Timeout and binding invalidation also end
conversations. Invalid initial datagrams and requests rejected before state
allocation write none. Reporting failure does not change admission.

This operational event is not a kernel access-audit record and does not
satisfy SACL audit requirements. It contains no password, shared secret,
private key, raw credential packet, or disclosed claim values.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The radiusd service account emitting the event, not the Wi-Fi user.
field: source.radiusd.username              optional
  Present after a valid UTF-8 inner username reaches credential verification.
field: object.radiusd.attempt.guid          required
field: object.radiusd.client.id             required
field: object.radiusd.network.id            required
field: object.radiusd.canonical-name        optional
  Present only after authd verified the credential, including later denials.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  Present together with the canonical name; the verified user's SID.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: authentication-failed | permission-denied | missing-context | authority-unavailable | kernel-api-unavailable | access-check-error | conversation-limit | timed-out | binding-changed | protocol-error | undelivered | allowance-exhausted | accounting-unavailable
  closed: false

field: object.radiusd.progress.sequence      optional
field: object.radiusd.progress.stage         optional
field: object.radiusd.last-stage             optional
field: object.radiusd.method                 optional
field: object.radiusd.elapsed-ms             optional
field: object.radiusd.retransmissions        optional
field: object.authentication.operation.guid  optional
field: object.radiusd.client.configuration-id optional
field: object.radiusd.network.configuration-id optional
field: object.radiusd.authentication-profile.id optional
field: object.radiusd.config.fingerprint     optional
field: object.radiusd.config.saved-fingerprint optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.rule.id     optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.profile.id  optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.fingerprint optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.vlan        optional
field: object.radiusd.reply                  optional
field: object.radiusd.diagnostics.truncated  optional
field: source.address                       optional
field: source.radiusd.station               optional
field: object.radiusd.progress.result        optional
field: object.radiusd.client.name optional
field: object.radiusd.network.name optional
field: object.radiusd.authentication-profile.name optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.profile.name optional
field: object.radiusd.assignment.rule.name optional
field: outcome.detail                       optional

--- event radiusd.configuration.loaded
tier: standard
gating: startup and observed configuration changes or transitions to unavailable
cardinality: once per validated activation or observed transition to invalid configuration

The service activated configuration or paused admissions because it could not.

An activation validates Registry configuration copied from one read-only
snapshot, then separately loads its referenced credential files. A failure
retains old sockets and bounded conversations but blocks new admissions and
cached success replies until validation recovers.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
field: config.root                          required
  Always Machine\Software\Radius.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: invalid-or-unavailable
  closed: false

--- event radiusd.accounting.health.changed
tier: standard
gating: accounting health observed at five-second intervals
cardinality: once on the first observation and each observed health transition

Accounting availability changed.

Success means accounting is off or its validated listeners and ledger are
available. It does not establish that a device delivered every report.
Failure covers invalid configuration, unavailable listeners, and storage
failures. Inspect the protected local accounting status for diagnostics.

The event contains the service actor and health outcome only. Personal
accounting history, identifiers, addresses, and usage remain in the protected
ledger. Rebuild does not replay this event. Submission is best effort.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The radiusd service account, never a network user's SID.
field: outcome.success                      required
